Clinical Course: The normal gut flora has been destroyed, allowing a toxin-producing bacteria to thrive. Hydration is the critical bridge until specific, targeted oral antibiotics can be initiated to eradicate the overgrowth.

SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Under no circumstances should you take pharmacy medications designed to stop diarrhea. This will trap the bacterial toxins in your colon, causing the bowel to expand dangerously and potentially rupture.

PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The previous antibiotics killed your good gut bacteria. We must replace your lost fluids with specific electrolytes right now, and avoid stopping the diarrhea, so the toxins can be flushed out while we wait for the lab results.
Actionable Steps: Drink 250ml of rehydration fluid after every loose stool. Wash hands strictly with soap and water; alcohol gels do not kill these specific bacterial spores.

